      <title>Aren’t Martyrs Automatically Canonized?</title>
      <link>https://www.franciscanmedia.org/ask-a-franciscan/arent-martyrs-automatically-canonized/</link>
      <description>Q: The feast of Saint Charles Lwanga and companion martyrs (June 3) recently raised a question for me. On July 17, 1794, 16 Carmelite nuns were guillotined in Compiègne, France, for their faith. As a secular Carmelite, I have always considered them a beacon of love and uncompromising faith. Doesn't the fact that they were martyred for their faith automatically make them saints? Why would any miracles be needed?</description>
